jane_cust: hey @support — we just started getting JSON parsing failures from the /v1/generate endpoint after flipping on structured_output. stacktrace says: \"invalid_type: expected number, got string at $.items[0].price\". our schema expects price:number

maya_support: thanks for the report — can you paste a minimal repro request + the response body you received? do you have a request_id or invocation id?

jane_cust: request_id=rid_01G9XKQZ. here's a minimal curl we used (sensitive bits redacted):

curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate \
 -H 'Authorization: Bearer REDACTED' \
 -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
 -d '{
  "model": "open-structured-1",
  "structured_schema": {"type":"object","properties":{"items":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"price":{"type":"number"},"name":{"type":"string"},"is_active":{"type":"boolean"},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["live","draft"]}},"required":["price"]}}},
  "input": "Return items list with price, name, is_active, status."
}'

and the actual model response we got: 

{
  "items": [
    {"price": "12.99", "name": "Widget", "is_active": "true", "status": "LIVE"}
  ]
}

maya_support: got it. so price and is_active are strings, and status enum is uppercase. that explains the validator error. two immediate asks: 1) did this start happening after toggling structured_output? 2) can you share a small sample of your prompt or schema injection — sometimes examples trigger stringified numbers.

jane_cust: yes it started after enabling structured_output last night. we didn't change prompt much, just added the schema field. here's the shortest prompt fragment: 

"Return JSON array of items. price should be numeric. is_active true/false. status live/draft."

samir_support: quick repro attempt on our side — i reproduced number-as-string with the exact schema + short prompt. Model sometimes quotes numbers when it decides to output them as strings. this is a common pattern if examples or wording use quotes.

ingrid_engineer: tagging from eng-runtime — ingrid here. thanks for the thread and the request_id. i pulled the payload for rid_01G9XKQZ from logs. model output tokens indeed include quotes around 12.99 and true. validator throws on strict JSON schema number/boolean types. two parallel paths:
1) short-term (workaround): post-process response to coerce types (parseFloat for numeric-like strings, /^(true|false)$/i for booleans, normalize enum casing). i can share a tiny helper script.
2) mid-term (product): we should add a configurable tolerant parsing option for structured_output that attempts type coercion and enum case-insensitive matching before failing. i'll open an RFC and a bug for the strict validator behavior.

maya_support: jane — do you prefer we enable a tenant-level tolerant parsing toggle for you while eng works on the RFC?

jane_cust: yes please. enabling tolerant parsing would be great — our prod needs to be unblocked.

ingrid_engineer: ok marking this P2. created ENG-9874 and linked request_id. estimated patch for the toggle in hosted: 48h for rollout to canary, 5 business days for full rollout. i'll also add an option to emit a validation report showing which fields were coerced.

samir_support: workaround helper (node) — paste into your code temporarily: 

```js
function coerceStructured(obj, schema) {
  // naive coercion: numbers in strings -> numbers, 'true'/'false' -> booleans, enum strings -> lowercase match
  if (Array.isArray(obj)) return obj.map(o=>coerceStructured(o,schema));
  if (obj && typeof obj === 'object') {
    const out = {}
    for (const k in obj) {
      let v = obj[k];
      if (typeof v === 'string') {
        if (/^-?\\d+\\.?\\d*$/.test(v)) v = parseFloat(v);
        else if (/^(true|false)$/i.test(v)) v = v.toLowerCase() === 'true';
        else v = v;
      }
      out[k] = v;
    }
    return out;
  }
  return obj;
}
```

maya_support: i've opened ticket TKT-5421 on your account to flip tolerant_parsing=true for your workspace. you'll see a console flag in ~5 mins. please redeploy and test the same request id.

deploy-bot: Deployment succeeded: feature-toggle.tolerant_parsing enabled for workspace ws_janecorp at 2026-03-17T14:12:03Z :rocket:

jane_cust: confirmed — after enabling the toggle the same response is accepted and our app no longer errors. thanks team! :tada: any ETA on the RFC/patch?
\
ingrid_engineer: RFC and bug created (ENG-9874). i'll follow up with engineering schedule in ENG backlog grooming tomorrow. aiming for a formal config + validator improvement in next minor release. will loop you in.
